{"name":"Limerick","hex":"#76857b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Limerick","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A county of Ireland.","A city in County Limerick."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Limerick"}],"entries":[{"title":"Limerick","blocks":[{"text":"Limerick is a city in western Ireland, in County Limerick. It is in the province of Munster and is in the Mid-West which comprises part of the Southern Region. With a population of 102,287 at the 2022 census, Limerick is the third-most populous urban area in Ireland, and the fourth-most populous city on the island of Ireland. It was founded by Scandinavian settlers in 812, during the Viking Age."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Limerick_r%C3%ADo_%2846531600435%29.jpg/330px-Limerick_r%C3%ADo_%2846531600435%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limerick","wikidata":"Q133315"},{"title":"Limerick (Dáil constituency)","blocks":[{"text":"Limerick was a parliamentary constituency represented in Dáil Éireann, the lower house of the Irish parliament or Oireachtas elected on the system of proportional representation by means of the single transferable vote (PR-STV). From 1923 to 1948, it represented the whole city and county of Limerick. On its second creation, from 2011 to 2016, it represented the rural part of the county of Limerick, other than in its neighbouring constituencies of Kerry North–West Limerick and Limerick City."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Limerick_D%C3%A1il_constituency_2011.png/330px-Limerick_D%C3%A1il_constituency_2011.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limerick_(D%C3%A1il_constituency)","wikidata":"Q6549238"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/King_John%27s_Castle_at_Twilight_Hou